arXiv:2611.30526v1 Announce Type: new 
Abstract: In this paper we aim to study in a unified fashion existence and regularity properties of solutions to a very general class of Dirichlet boundary value problems such as \begin{equation}\label{P1abs}\tag{1}
  \begin{cases}
  - \mbox{div}\left(\displaystyle \phi(|\nabla u|) \nabla u\right) = f(x) &\quad \mbox{in } \Omega,\newline
  u = 0 &\quad \mbox{on } \partial \Omega,
  \end{cases} \end{equation} where $\phi:[0,\infty)\to [0,\infty)$ is any function such that $\phi(s)s \in C((0,\infty))$ is a non-decreasing function which tends to $1$ as $s\to\infty$. Among others, most of the far-famed operators derived from functionals with linear growth, as for instance the $1$-Laplacian and the minimal surface operator are included in our model. Under suitable assumptions on the data we prove existence and regularity results for problem \eqref{P1abs} which recover the sharp thresholds known in the model cases.

arXiv:2611.30561v1 Announce Type: new 
Abstract: In this paper, we study positive solutions to the problem
  \begin{equation*}
  -\Delta u = |x|^{-s_2}u^{2^*(s_2)-1} - \la |x|^{-s_1}u^{p-1} \quad \text{in }\Om, \qquad u=0 \quad \text{on }\partial\Om,
  \end{equation*}
  where $\Om\subset\R^N$ ($N\ge 3$) is a bounded domain with $0\in\partial\Om$, $0\le s_1<s_2<2$, $2^*(s)=\frac{2(N-s)}{N-2}$, $2^*(s_2)<p<2^*(s_1)$, and $\la>0$. This is the Li--Lin open problem \cite{LL} in the form studied by Cerami, Zhong, and Zou \cite{CZZ} and by Tang and Tang \cite{TT1}. Assume that $\partial\Om$ is $C^{1,\alpha}$ near $0$ with a leading term of homogeneity $1+\alpha$, and set $\theta=\frac{(N-2)(2^*(s_1)-p)}{2}$. We prove that a solution exists for every $\la>0$ if $\theta>\alpha$ and the $\alpha$-mean curvature of $\partial\Om$ at $0$ is negative, whereas $\la^*=\sup\{\la>0:\text{a solution exists}\}$ is finite if $\theta\le\alpha$, without any curvature assumption. For $\alpha=1$, this removes the restriction to almost every $\la$ in \cite[Theorem 1.6]{CZZ}, answers a question of Zou \cite{Z}, and disproves the conjecture in \cite[Remark 1.7]{TT1}. The proofs rely on a scale-invariant estimate uniform in $\la$, a Hadamard-type identity for the half-space extremal and a localized Pohozaev identity combined with sharp decay estimates. Notably, no regularity of $\partial\Om$ is required away from $0$.

